  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most informative first experiment should establish whether the core multimodal fusion hypothesis is viable and set a strong reference point. config_009 (multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, concat) tests the primary study hypothesis—combining RNA and image modalities—using the stronger image encoder (ViT-L) to probe the performance ceiling, a well-established RNA encoder (scvi_n200), and the simplest fusion (concat) to avoid confounding from complex aggregation or weighting. Starting with a strong multimodal configuration lets me immediately exploit a promising direction if it performs well, or pivot toward single-modality baselines or alternative fusion strategies if it underperforms. Under a 10-experiment budget, establishing the multimodal ceiling early maximizes the remaining 9 experiments for targeted refinement."
}

